What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/180f0000.wifi/transfer_mode
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	X20 development project
Description:
		Development control for the MT6797 dedicated WLAN AHB HIF.
		Read returns "pio" or "dma", the cumulative count of completed
		DMA transfers and the channel fault flag. Write "pio" or "dma"
		to select packet FIFO transport for the next WLAN session.
		Register accesses always use PIO. PIO is the default.

		Changing mode while the HIF is claimed, or while a failed DMA
		channel still needs its clock, returns EBUSY. Selecting DMA
		without the dedicated channel resource returns EOPNOTSUPP.
		A DMA timeout fails the current session; it never retries an
		incomplete packet through PIO. This interface is for bring-up
		and does not establish WLAN firmware or data-plane readiness.

                The X20 storage DT selects DMA at probe with the optional
                mediatek,use-dma boolean on the WLAN HIF and BTIF nodes.
                An absent property retains PIO for diagnostic DTs. Selecting
                DMA requires a successfully allocated hardware DMA buffer;
                the existing sysfs controls remain available while unclaimed.
